# ─── Canonical host ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The netlify.app subdomain serves a complete working copy of the site.
# Left alone, Google can index it as duplicate content and split ranking
# signals across two hostnames. The trailing ! forces the rule even when
# a matching file exists.
https://fsrivercityrealty.netlify.app/*  https://fsrivercityrealty.com/:splat  301!
http://fsrivercityrealty.netlify.app/*   https://fsrivercityrealty.com/:splat  301!

# ─── Old WordPress URLs → new site ───────────────────────────────
# Source: fsrivercityrealty.com/wp-sitemap-posts-page-1.xml (10 URLs)
# 301 = permanent. Preserves search ranking through the migration.

# The three tips pages are the only real content the old site had, and
# they all map to the combined Buying & Selling guide.
/tips-for-buyers                 /pages/guide.html                301
/tips-for-buyers/                /pages/guide.html                301
/tips-for-sellers                /pages/guide.html                301
/tips-for-sellers/               /pages/guide.html                301
/tips-for-buyers/find-a-builder  /pages/guide.html                301
/tips-for-buyers/find-a-builder/ /pages/guide.html                301

/contact                         /pages/contact.html              301
/contact/                        /pages/contact.html              301

# Seller valuation — IDX hosts the tool, so this goes to the subdomain
# rather than to a page on this site.
/free-home-evaluation   https://homes.fsrivercityrealty.com/idx/homevaluation   301
/free-home-evaluation/  https://homes.fsrivercityrealty.com/idx/homevaluation   301

# The old /cities/ and /counties/ pages were link directories into IDX.
# Map Search replaces both and lets the visitor pick either.
/cities     https://homes.fsrivercityrealty.com/idx/map/mapsearch   301
/cities/    https://homes.fsrivercityrealty.com/idx/map/mapsearch   301
/counties   https://homes.fsrivercityrealty.com/idx/map/mapsearch   301
/counties/  https://homes.fsrivercityrealty.com/idx/map/mapsearch   301

# There is no newly-listed saved link in IDX account 3683, so this points
# at a direct query instead: residential, active, listed in the last 7 days.
/newly-listed-homes-for-sale   https://homes.fsrivercityrealty.com/idx/results/homes?idxID=d124&pt=1&add=7&a_propStatus[]=Active&srt=newest   301
/newly-listed-homes-for-sale/  https://homes.fsrivercityrealty.com/idx/results/homes?idxID=d124&pt=1&add=7&a_propStatus[]=Active&srt=newest   301

# ─── Old IDX URLs on the main domain ─────────────────────────────
# The previous site served IDX pages from fsrivercityrealty.com rather than
# the homes. subdomain. Same structure as CFR, which got these rules first.
# Wildcards rather than one rule per URL — :splat carries the rest of the
# path and Netlify preserves the query string automatically.
#
# These do NOT touch /idx-wrapper/ — that path is matched only by a literal
# /idx/ prefix, which /idx-wrapper/ does not have.
/idx/*  https://homes.fsrivercityrealty.com/idx/:splat  301
/i/*    https://homes.fsrivercityrealty.com/i/:splat    301

# NOTE: /idx-wrapper/ is deliberately NOT redirected. It is served by
# idx-wrapper/index.html so IDX Broker's Global wrapper URL keeps working
# unchanged after DNS moves. IDX cannot follow redirects.
